  "verdict": "The EDA found utilisation U-shaped rather than monotone. In the PD curve of UTIL_MEAN the minimum is 0.2041 at UTIL_MEAN = 0.084, it is interior, the curve falls +0.0239 into it from the left end and rises +0.0395 out of it to the right end, so the U-shape SURVIVES in the fitted model and not only in the raw default rates. The empirical training deciles of UTIL_MEAN move 0.264 -> minimum 0.140 (decile 4) -> 0.334, i.e. the same shape. This matters for the report's argument for tree-based methods: a linear model in UTIL_MEAN can only be monotone — the logistic regression is forced into a single coefficient of +0.288 per SD (odds ratio 1.334), which has to average the falling and the rising half of the curve into one number, while the booster fits the fall and the rise separately. Note that the EDA measured the U-shape on UTIL_1, which correlates r = 0.91 with UTIL_MEAN."
 },
